Z||000000||Ralfy9862||07-06-2001||06:09 PM||||engine Turns over but wont start. the only way for me to start the car is to spray that spray petroleum stuff into the air box then it will start and run fine.but the when i turn it off it wont start again ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Steve Normington||07-06-2001||06:22 PM||||Does the fuel pump run when you turn the key to on? You should hear the pump going for 2 seconds. Also, what does the oil pressure read as you are cranking it w/o starting? If you kill the engine and immediantly restart it, what happens?||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||07-06-2001||07:37 PM||||Four things an engine needs in order to run (for the most part)..<BR>1. Spark...check it<BR>2. Air...usually not a prob, but check anyway<BR>3. Compression....pray this is never your prob<BR>4. Fuel delivery...<B>Id bet this is your prob...</B>..check the "whine' of the fuel pump at pre start up, may also want to replace oil sending unit (it also runs the fuel pump)...OSU is cheap and extremely easy fix. Good luck, M7F||||reg||1
